["RHODE 2014-2015 SGP ANALYSES\n NECAP TO PARCC TRANSITION\n\n Damian W Betebenner\nNational Center for the Improvement of Educational Assessment\n Providence, RI November 23rd, 2015","TOPICS FOR DISCUSSION\n\n• Student growth review\n\n• Analyses and diagnostics associated with the 2014-2015.","STUDENT GROWTH IN RHODE ISLAND\n• Analyses conducted for rst time in 2008 and have been\n performed annually since. Last performed for Fall 2013 NECAP\n administration.\n\n• Analyses conducted for both Mathematics and Reading.\n\n• Student growth percentiles were calculated and used, particularly\n as part of teacher evaluation work conducted under RttT.\n\n• Student growth projections were calculated but not used as part\n of accountability or reporting.targets for typical and higher growth\n a year in advance.\n\n fi","THE TRANSITION TO PARCC\n\n• SGP analyses are norm-referenced and don’t require a vertical\n scale to be conducted. Depending upon whether results are\n disseminated, a likely cause of confusion: “How can you calculate\n growth across two different tests?”\n\n• Other PARCC SGP states we’re conducting analyses for:\n Massachusetts, New Jersey, Colorado\n\n• The Center conducted meetings with both SBAC and PARCC\n consortium members discussing issues related to calculating and\n using growth during assessment transitions.","THE TRANSITION TO PARCC\nCORRELATIONS PRIOR YEAR TO CURRENT\n Grades Grades Grades Grades Grades\n 3 to 4 4 to 5 5 to 6 6 to 7 7 to 8\n\n 2010-11 to 0.87 (Math) 0.86 (Math) 0.87 (Math) 0.88 (Math) 0.87 (Math)\n 2011-2012 0.80 (Read) 0.77 (Read) 0.80 (Read) 0.82 (Read) 0.83 (Read)\n\n 2011-12 to 0.87 (Math) 0.87 (Math) 0.87 (Math) 0.88 (Math) 0.87 (Math)\n 2012-13 0.81 (Read) 0.79 (Read) 0.81 (Read) 0.80 (Read) 0.83 (Read)\n\n 2012-13 to 0.87 (Math) 0.88 (Math) 0.87 (Math) 0.88 (Math) 0.87 (Math)\n 2013-14 0.80 (Read) 0.78 (Read) 0.80 (Read) 0.81 (Read) 0.82 (Read)\n\n 2013-14 to 0.81(Math)\n 0.72 (Math RR)\n 0.79 (Math)\n 0.71 (Math RR)\n 0